    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and working. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Bug:** The `frai gate init --ci` command was not creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` file, even though the same command works fine when calling `frai-gate` directly.\n\n**Root Cause:** The frai CLI's gate command handler was using commander's argument parsing with `[args...]`, which wasn't properly forwarding the `--ci` flag to the frai-gate subprocess.\n\n**Fix:** In `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`, I modified the gate command handler to extract raw arguments directly from `process.argv` instead of relying on commander's parsed arguments. This ensures all flags are passed through unchanged to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Key Change:**\n- Replaced commander's parsed `args` parameter with direct extraction from `process.argv`\n- Find the 'gate' command in process.argv and pass everything after it to spawnSync\n- This bypasses commander's parsing for gate subcommand arguments\n\n**Verification:**\n- \u2705 Rebuilt the frai package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- \u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` and confirmed both files are now created:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`",
